a.q('resolution_effect_limit',['product_resolution'],'Producing a lock neither installs a product nor alters workspace binding.',[g(1,379,382)])
a.c('workspace_binding','Exact immutable workspace binding','workspace.bind consumes admitted workspace, exact verified product set and resolved lock and returns immutable binding/manifest or typed refusal.',[g(1,384,395)])
a.q('binding_immutability',['workspace_binding'],'Binding cannot install missing products, admit contributions, start traversal or broaden selection. Changed products/lock/authority/root set requires separately admitted identity, never earlier mutation/global current pointer. Each workspace/execution invocation selects exactly one binding; continued spine change also needs exact covering reprice. Ordinary observation/replay/process/file/artifact changes do not mutate or invalidate it.',[g(1,384,395)])
a.c('catalog_operations','Catalog admit, read and view','catalog.admit consumes exact binding/lock/verified descriptors+manifests; list/describe are project.read projections; catalog.view constructs narrowing-only view from admitted catalog and allowlist.',[g(1,397,414)])
a.q('catalog_disposition_and_effects',['catalog_operations'],'Admission returns catalog identity and typed admitted/rejected/incompatible/conflicting/unready/unresolved row results without invocation, session widening, traversal events or binding change. Reads preserve kind/handle/owner/readiness/eligibility/callability/compatibility/session visibility/contract/provenance as applicable. View returns identity and typed unknown/duplicate/ambiguous/unauthorized/inadmissible/not-ready residuals without widening/changing workspace catalog.',[g(1,397,414)])
a.c('graph_function_invocation','run.invoke invoke variant','Direct invocation selects explicit canonical admitted GraphFunction handle published by one admitted GTL program with declared input, exact immutable binding and session policy/capability inputs.',[g(1,416,429)])
a.q('invoke_static_runtime_partition',['graph_function_invocation'],'ABG consumes typed non-lowering validator membership/contract judgment without reinterpreting or recomputing it, then admits concrete input against contracts/catalog eligibility/binding/policy/capability/authority before one GraphCall. Direct invoke accepts/requires no root_mode/until/start grammar and does not require or synthesize evaluateNext, One Surface or ConstructionIntent. When realizing evaluateNext-selected One Surface action, exact function narrows published ActionCatalog and binds admitted selected intent without bypassing evaluateNext. Both paths return contract-required call/Run/result-or-stop/evidence/replay refs, never equate function with program or call non-GraphFunction kinds.',[g(1,416,437)])
a.c('evidence_projection','Evidence projection','project.read evidence is read-only for supported Run, GraphCall, result, assessment, witness, install or release identities, retaining evidence identity/kind/subject/content-or-artifact/producer/basis/published digest/provenance/replay.',[g(1,439,444)])
a.q('no_adapter_evidence_manufacture',['evidence_projection'],'Adapter-local observations cannot manufacture evidence.',[g(1,439,444)])
a.c('product_materialization','Product materialization and install','context_bootstrap, configuration and product.install are typed public operations with explicit admitted inputs and manifests/provenance.',[g(1,446,465)])
a.q('materialization_effect_boundaries',['product_materialization'],'Bootstrap accepts admitted target and exact binding, reports created/refreshed/preserved/refused surfaces, neither replaces project authority nor selects mutable source as installed truth. Install accepts exact artifact/contracts and reports verification/materialization/installed/provenance; failed verification yields no installed/bound/admitted/callable truth and bind/admit remain separate. Configuration accepts admitted contract, binding and inputs, returns exact content/validation/provenance/residuals; no mutable source defaults or runtime truth change merely from construction.',[g(1,446,465)])
a.c('release_snapshot','release.snapshot variants','published_rc or tapped_release consumes exact qualification/law basis and authenticated native same-basis green non-bypassed verdict, preserving native qualification/acceptance authority.',[g(1,467,485)])
a.q('rc_publication_and_tap',['release_snapshot'],'published_rc only accepts pre_rc_candidate and basis-bound prospective RC identity, publishing exact qualified bytes unchanged. tapped_release only accepts exact installed_rc, matching native green verdict, complete immutable RC lineage and actual human Product-authority acceptance of unchanged RC; report existing cut/artifact/snapshot and write only external acceptance/evidence addendum. No second cut/snapshot/package, rename or selector move. Caller green/accepted flags confer no authority. Return exact immutable identities/digests, qualification/applicable acceptance disposition, residuals/provenance or typed refusal.',[g(1,467,483)])
a.q('partial_release_effect_receipt',['release_snapshot'],'Any partial publication/addendum retains actual effect receipt and unresolved state for exact reacquisition; neither complete release success nor effect-free refusal may be claimed.',[g(1,483,485)])
a.c('workspace_create_open','Workspace create/open','Create accepts admitted target and explicit clean/imported authority mode; open reads existing target workspace/product truth with stable authority and current binding/config state.',[g(1,487,499)])
a.q('workspace_operation_boundaries',['workspace_create_open'],'Create returns identity and creation/bootstrap eligibility without install/bind/catalog admission, omitted project-authority scaffold or runtime events. Open returns typed missing/malformed/stale/incompatible/ready without silent install/rebind/re-resolution/admission/widening/start.',[g(1,487,499)])
a.c('public_invocation_outcome','PublicInvocation<K> and PublicOutcome<K>','Versioned host-neutral descriptor and result/refusal/nonterminal family for every public operation carry schema/definition identity/version/digest, operation+variant, exact InvocationAuthority and indexed required/forbidden workspace/binding/lock/view/program/function/input/payload/policy/capability/actor/transport truth; run.invoke adds applicable interface or public start and scope+target+until.',[g(1,501,511)])
a.l('public_descriptor_transport',['public_invocation_outcome'],['Native caller/CLI/host constructs or transports same admitted descriptor and transports corresponding outcome.','Wrap host metadata without changing public meaning.'],['Include worker invocation, private frame/frontier/continuation, adapter graph logic, event authority, retry, selection, evaluation or closure decisions.','Let ingress or adapter construct outcome instead of owning semantic function.'],[g(1,513,520)])
a.q('public_definition_authority',['public_operations','public_invocation_outcome'],'All operations use exact abg.operation.* and addressable request/result/error/invocation schemas. Definition row owns defaults, closed variants/value domains, actor/mutation class, refusals/disposition/exits. Flags/overloads/projections only bind rows and cannot complete absent meanings. Legacy operation identities or parallel compatibility register fail publication/conformance.',[g(1,522,529)])
a.q('public_operation_acceptance',['public_operations'],'Completion requires installed source-blind SDK/CLI consumer to create/open; resolve/verify/install/bind products/admit catalog; inspect/narrow; noncallable apply; program-owned function invoke/start; read status/result/evidence/replay/gaps/actions; pending-interaction response; lawful continue/restart to convergence; assessment/witness/conformance/install/materialization/release via exact definitions; equivalent typed dispositions with no adapter runtime/orchestration ownership or legacy/parallel register.',[g(2,533,553)],uncertainty='The acceptance list includes interaction.respond; release-scoped applicability is controlled outside this subsection and native response is elsewhere reserved for 5.1.')
a.u('operation_acceptance_release_scope','public_operation_acceptance','This acceptance checklist includes native interaction response and continuation, while supplied public-contract purpose reserves response-driven same-Run resumption for 5.1.','Do not infer these checklist items as unconditional 5.0 supported behavior; re-enter release applicability and reconcile wording.',[g(2,547,553),g(4,21,25)])
a.c('public_contract_catalog','Addressable public contract catalog','Active 5.0 family names a static versioned installed-manifest section locating native exports, serialization schemas, closed vocabularies, conformance corpora, operations and capabilities without source/ticket/history/implementation inference; not hosted service or second checker.',[g(3,3,7),g(4,13,19)])
a.q('capability_release_claims',['public_contract_catalog'],'Human hold/block, attribution and typed refusal remain 5.0; native response and response-driven same-Run resume are 5.1. Capability claims distinguish retained versus reserved definitions; schema/binding presence alone claims no support.',[g(4,21,25)])
a.q('manifest_bootstrap_fields',['public_contract_catalog'],'Each conforming 5.0+ product root contains product-toolchain-manifest.json with kind=abg_product_toolchain_manifest, schemaVersion, productId, packageName, packageVersion, productContentDigest and one publicContractCatalog; missing/malformed/duplicate/digest-incoherent fields fail verification. Catalog carries schemaVersion, catalogId/version/digest, catalogSchemaPath/digest and rows; paths are product-root-relative, never absolute, parent traversal or symlink-dependent source locators.',[g(5,29,41)])
a.q('canonical_digest_law',['public_contract_catalog'],'Digests are sha256: plus 64 lowercase hex; JSON identity uses RFC8785 JCS UTF-8. Product digest hashes sorted relative-path/file-sha256 inventory excluding manifest and mutable state. Catalog digest hashes canonical catalog minus own field. Schema/asset hashes use exact bytes. Serialized/schema/vocabulary/corpus contractDigest equals canonical asset digest; native typed groups hash published canonical export-path/declaration-relative-path/declaration-sha256 inventory, not loader order/source paths. Final canonical manifest digest is stored in binding/install record outside the manifest; no self-digest field.',[g(5,43,58)])
a.q('contract_row_identity_and_locator',['public_contract_catalog'],'Rows carry stable contractId/version/digest/kind/owner/requirement authority/capability identities and native package-export-symbol locator, canonical relative asset/media-schema/version/digest locator, or both. Every serialized public request/result/event/manifest/descriptor/contribution/lock/replay/conformance needs asset/schema locator; stronger native constraints cannot contradict serialization. Exact contract/capability identity cannot resolve to different schema/symbol/semantics/digest; removal/semantic change needs new version or explicit supersession; ambient package/source paths cannot select it.',[g(5,60,77)])
a.u('catalog_external_authorities','public_contract_catalog','Referenced PRODUCT release boundaries, PUBLIC-CONTRACTS definitions, install/policy/mapping derivations and external RFC8785 are not supplied as complete definitions here.','Retain declared references and exact digest rule without fabricating cross-document endpoints or demonstrating implementation conformance.',[g(3,6),g(4,21,25),g(5,43,58)])
